 m will not be silenced! Join San Francisco Shakespeare Festival on Saturda
 y\, September 26 for an afternoon of Antony + Cleopatra\, followed by a Ne
 w Orleans-style procession down the Embarcadero. Make a full day of it or 
 join us for the procession at 4pm. Make a sign. See the play. Take it to t
 he streets. ____ 12–2 PM | Sign Making Start at the Free Shakespeare in 
 the Park stage in Sue Bierman Park and make your own sign. We’ll provide
  the supplies! 2–3:45 PM | Antony & Cleopatra Stay for the Free Shakespe
 are in the Park performance of “Antony + Cleopatra.” 4–5 PM | Proces
 sion After the performance\, join a second line procession led by Jazz Maf
 ia with Cleopatra in the lead. This will be a short\, accessible processio
 n along the Embarcadero\, culminating at the Ferry Building. Come as you a
 re! No special clothing or supplies are required. The procession is free a
